implementationPlan.note:
QA reopen 1, the fix (security issue at moe-agent.sh:534). Under the marker, protected_pin_interpreters now pins only a file that the NAME `node` resolves to. use_node prepends only the pinned file's dir, and moe-call.sh find_node (`command -v node`) and env-node shebangs look up the name.
- exe='.exe' on msys/cygwin, '' elsewhere.
- MOE_NODE_COMMAND and the managed runtime must have basename `node` (msys/cygwin: also `node.exe`): `case "${candidate##*/}" in node|"node$exe") ;; *) continue ;; esac`. Any other name is skipped like N3's untrusted overrides, so the order is managed runtime, then the PATH scan. No new output.
- The node PATH scan passes $exe as protected_path_lookup's extension list. On msys/cygwin a dir holding only node.cmd is skipped.
Scope note: that last item goes one step past QA's literal text but closes the same root cause. Git Bash probe (scratch, removed):
  - the old default lookup pinned d1/node.cmd;
  - `PATH=d1:… command -v node` does not find node.cmd;
  - the new lookup pins d2/node;
  - the CLI resolver still finds claude.cmd;
  - nodejs.exe and node.cmd overrides are skipped; node.exe and node are accepted.
python3 is unchanged: nothing looks python3 up by name after the pin (grep: bare python3/py/python only in legacy find_python).
GREEN: `bash -n` ok. All bash rows of protected-agent-command.test.mjs: 39/39 pass, including N5 4/4 (red before) and N1 3/3 with daemon.json and the deregister proof. Log: /tmp/moe-64809-s3-green.log.

