- The node.exe half runs the ps1 rows and slices under Windows PowerShell 5.1 and pwsh 7. Report pass and skip counts per engine; a skipped PowerShell 5.1 row is a failure.
- Mutation spot-checks, on a scratch copy of scripts/ on /mnt/d outside the repo, never the live wrappers. Report each:
  - restore `command -v node` in the pin: N1/N3 go red;
  - drop the alias: ps1 N1 goes red;
  - restore moe-call.sh's python3 probe: N1/M1 go red;
  - drop a TOML .Replace: S1 goes red.

reopenReason:
Reviewed completion 0863b6c6 (on moe/work-2026-10-24; +295/-68, net 227, the 4 approved files; ps1 BOM kept). I re-ran the exact verification command on a git-archive snapshot of 0863b6c6. It exits 0: WSL 151 tests (125 pass, 0 fail, 26 skip), Windows 210 (175 pass, 0 fail, 35 skip), parity PASS. Legacy, the ps1 pins, the moe-call python3 skip and the N0 guard are good.

REJECT: sh breaks the contract's rules that sh "includes moe-call.sh's deregister" and that "nothing reachable only through an empty, '.', relative or in-project PATH entry ever runs".

Take a trusted absolute MOE_NODE_COMMAND whose basename is not `node`:
- protected_pin_interpreters (moe-agent.sh:534) pins it;
- use_node prepends only its dir;
- moe-call.sh find_node (line 119, `command -v node`) and env-node shebangs look up the NAME `node`, so the next entry, '.' or empty, wins.

REPRO, the committed harness plus one scratch row:
- plantInterpreters; daemon.json '{}'; a trusted claude stub;
- MOE_NODE_COMMAND=<root>/altnode/nodejs (a symlink to process.execPath);
- PATH ['.' or '', fx.trusted, ...TAIL], nodeDir:false.

ran.log = 'project node' for both entries. It comes from cleanup_temp's moe-call.sh deregister_worker (PATH=<altnode>:.:…, cwd=project, `command -v node` = ./node). Plan step 3's "its dir goes first on PATH, so shebangs and moe-call.sh find the same node" holds only for a file named node.

N1 missed it because its fixture has no .moe/daemon.json, so moe-call.sh exits at its daemon check (lines 213-217) before running node (line 219). With daemon.json '{}', the committed code makes a 5th runtime call (the deregister through the pinned node) and N1 stays green, so the stronger row works.

Non-blocking: POSIX pwsh does not prepend the pinned dir. That is the documented "other PATH tools" residual, handed to epic-final.

